  "design": {
    "decision": "Your team plays a two-suit hand every round, void in [♣] and [♥], so it bids on ruffing power and [♦] length, and every [♦] payoff becomes a build-around.",
    "opponent": "Shown on the first [♣] or [♥] lead; opponents hold all of those suits with nobody to follow, so they lead [♠] to strip trumps and attack the long [♦]s.",
    "rationale": "This is the legendary [♦] build-around, the broad version of ra-clubs-to-diamonds: two voids are a strong Spades edge on their own, and the combo with [♦] hold payoffs is deliberately explosive but needs a rare-plus-legendary assembly. Duplicate [♦] cards follow the kernel's existing tie rules for synthetic copies.",
